I'm trying to add Disqus to a bookdown site. The embedded Javascript code includes [Javascript configuration variables](https://help.disqus.com/en/articles/1717084-javascript-configuration-variables) that are [important for avoiding split threads and missing comments](https://help.disqus.com/en/articles/1717137-use-configuration-variables-to-avoid-split-threads-and-missing-comments). Thus "*[Disqus recommends] that you define the `PAGE_URL` and `PAGE_IDENTIFIER` configuration variables within the `disqus_config` section of your embed code.*" How can these be specified automatically?

Here's the relevant section of the embed code:

```
var disqus_config = function () {
    this.page.url = PAGE_URL;  // Replace PAGE_URL with your page's canonical URL variable
    this.page.identifier = PAGE_IDENTIFIER; // Replace PAGE_IDENTIFIER with your page's unique identifier variable
    };
```

For instance, the Disqus documentation notes that: "*These variables should be defined by using your CMS’ or platform’s dynamic values, if available. For example, the Disqus WordPress plugin defines these variables by default using the following PHP values:*"

```
this.page.url = '<?php echo get_permalink(); ?>';
this.page.identifier = '<?php echo dsq_identifier_for_post($post); ?>';
```

As noted [here](https://github.com/rstudio/bookdown/issues/81#issuecomment-356824941):
"*the embedded javascript code requires the url of the webpage (so the url of the page you're generating with bookdown). The domain can be indicated manually, since it is only known by the author, of course ; but what about the relative path of any given webpage? Is there any automatic way of generating it (i.e., something similar to a {{page.url}} liquid tag)?*"

This is a similar issue for adding Discourse: https://github.com/rstudio/bookdown/issues/81#issuecomment-356824941

